	<section class="section" style="max-width: 760px;">
		<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="subtitle">How Veltara Works handles your information on vectismail.com and when you buy or use Vectis Mail&trade;.</p>
		<p style="color: var(--sl-color-gray-3); font-size: 0.95rem;"><strong>Effective:</strong> 17 May 2026 &middot; <strong>Last updated:</strong> 17 May 2026</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">At a glance</h2>
		<p>The short version, then the detail:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>We don't run analytics, behavioural ad pixels, or third-party trackers on this site. No Google Analytics, no Facebook Pixel, no session-replay.</li>
			<li>We collect only what's needed to reply to enquiries, ship the product, and keep the lights on.</li>
			<li>Payments are handled by <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a> (the merchant of record) and <a href="https://stripe.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">Stripe</a> (the payment processor). We never see your card details.</li>
			<li>Once Vectis Mail runs on <em>your</em> server, the personal data your install processes (mailboxes, message content, recipient addresses) is controlled by you, not by us.</li>
			<li>You can email us at <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a> for any privacy question, data-subject request, or to exercise any right described below.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">1. Who we are</h2>
		<p>Vectis Mail is a product of <strong>Veltara Works&trade;</strong>, the trading entity that publishes this website. Veltara Works is an Australian operation; the principal contact is the founder, Ian Holt.</p>
		<p>For privacy matters specifically, please contact us at <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a> with "Privacy" in the subject line. We monitor this address daily and will respond within 30 days (usually within 2&ndash;3 business days). If you require postal correspondence, request the current registered address through that channel and we will provide it.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">2. Two distinct privacy contexts</h2>
		<p>Vectis Mail is a self-hosted product. This means there are two very different layers of data handling to keep straight:</p>
		<ol style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li><strong>vectismail.com itself</strong> &mdash; the marketing site, the contact form, the purchase journey. Veltara Works is the <em>controller</em> of any personal information collected here. The rest of this policy mostly describes this layer.</li>
			<li><strong>Your Vectis Mail server</strong> &mdash; once you install Vectis Mail on your own infrastructure and start operating mailboxes for your users, <em>you</em> are the controller of the personal data flowing through your install. Veltara Works is the software vendor &mdash; we wrote the code, but we don't see your users' mail. The licence verification call your install makes to <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ValidonX</a> every 5 minutes transmits only an opaque tenant identifier; it carries no mailbox lists, no message content, no recipient addresses, and no IP addresses of your users.</li>
		</ol>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">3. What we collect on vectismail.com</h2>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3a. Visiting the site</h3>
		<p>When you browse vectismail.com, our hosting provider (Cloudflare Pages) records the technical information any web server records to deliver pages and defend against abuse: your IP address, the time of the request, the URL you visited, the page that referred you, and the user-agent string your browser sends. This information lives in Cloudflare's logs &mdash; we don't aggregate it, profile you with it, or sell it. Cloudflare may set short-lived cookies (notably <code>__cf_bm</code>) to distinguish humans from automated traffic; these are strictly functional and expire within 30 minutes of your last visit.</p>
		<p>We do not load Google Analytics, Facebook Pixel, LinkedIn Insight, X (Twitter) tracking, Hotjar, FullStory, or any comparable behavioural-tracking script. The only third-party scripts on the page are Cloudflare's bot-management challenge runtime, loaded only if a request triggers it.</p>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3b. Using the contact form</h3>
		<p>If you submit the form at <a href="/contact" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">/contact</a>, we collect:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>Your name and email address</li>
			<li>The department you've selected (General Enquiries, Enterprise Sales, or Technical Support)</li>
			<li>Your message text</li>
		</ul>
		<p>That form posts to a small Cloudflare Pages Function, which forwards your message into the Vectis Mail server that runs <code>mail.vectismail.com</code>. From there it lands in the inbox of <code>hello@</code>, <code>sales@</code>, or <code>support@vectismail.com</code> depending on the department you chose. The data path is: <em>your browser &rarr; Cloudflare edge &rarr; mail.vectismail.com &rarr; mailbox</em>. We use this information to reply to your enquiry and keep an internal record of the conversation so we can pick up where we left off if you write again. We don't add you to a marketing list off the back of a support enquiry.</p>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3c. Buying a Vectis Pro subscription</h3>
		<p>Vectis Pro is purchased through ValidonX, our sister company, who handle subscription management and billing for the whole Veltara Works portfolio. ValidonX is the merchant of record. ValidonX uses Stripe to process card payments. We do not see, store, or process your payment card details; they go directly from your browser to Stripe.</p>
		<p>After payment, ValidonX issues you a tenant identifier, a licence key, and a service key, and emails them to you so you can paste them into the admin UI of your Vectis Mail install. We learn about your subscription only insofar as your install calls ValidonX every 5 minutes to confirm you still hold a valid licence. ValidonX has its own privacy policy at <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">validonx.com</a>; please consult it for the billing-side of the relationship.</p>

		<h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">3d. Email correspondence</h3>
		<p>If you email us at any address ending in <code>@vectismail.com</code>, we retain the message (and any reply we send) to maintain a continuous conversation thread. The retention rules for these mailboxes are set out in the Retention section below.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">4. What we don't collect</h2>
		<p>To be explicit about scope:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>We do not run analytics or fingerprinting scripts on vectismail.com.</li>
			<li>We do not buy advertising audience lists, retargeting cohorts, or third-party data enrichment.</li>
			<li>We do not load social-media share buttons that report your visit back to the social network ("Like" buttons, Twitter-share widgets, etc).</li>
			<li>We do not use session-replay tools (mouse-movement / scroll recording).</li>
			<li>We do not embed marketing automation pixels in our outbound emails.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">5. How we use your information</h2>
		<p>We use the information described in section 3 strictly to:</p>
		<ol style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>Reply to enquiries you've sent us through the contact form or by email.</li>
			<li>Provide and improve Vectis Mail in response to feedback (we may quote a problem you've reported back to ourselves anonymously when writing release notes; we won't name you publicly without permission).</li>
			<li>Operate the technical infrastructure (defend against abuse, debug errors, ship security updates).</li>
			<li>Comply with legal obligations &mdash; for example, retaining records relating to a paid subscription long enough to satisfy tax, contract, and consumer-law requirements.</li>
		</ol>
		<p>We do not, and have never, sold personal information.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">6. Who we share information with</h2>
		<p>We use a small number of carefully-chosen processors. Each is contracted to use information only on our instructions and only for the purposes described above:</p>

		<div class="feature-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); margin-top: 1rem;">
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>ValidonX</h3>
				<p><strong>Role:</strong> Merchant of record &amp; licensing platform.<br/>
				<strong>Location:</strong> Australia.<br/>
				<strong>What we share:</strong> When you start a Pro subscription, ValidonX receives the information you provide at checkout (name, billing email, payment method via Stripe). We additionally exchange opaque tenant identifiers so your install can verify your licence.<br/>
				<strong>Site:</strong> <a href="https://validonx.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">validonx.com</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Stripe, Inc.</h3>
				<p><strong>Role:</strong> Payment processor (used by ValidonX).<br/>
				<strong>Location:</strong> United States, with global infrastructure.<br/>
				<strong>What we share:</strong> Stripe receives the payment-card details you enter at checkout. We never see your card number, CVC, or expiry. Stripe self-certifies to the EU&ndash;US Data Privacy Framework.<br/>
				<strong>Site:</strong> <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">stripe.com/privacy</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>Cloudflare, Inc.</h3>
				<p><strong>Role:</strong> DNS, CDN, edge compute (Pages Functions), bot management.<br/>
				<strong>Location:</strong> United States, with worldwide edge infrastructure.<br/>
				<strong>What we share:</strong> Cloudflare processes connection metadata for every request to vectismail.com (IP, user-agent, requested URL). Cloudflare's role is covered by Standard Contractual Clauses where required and by their own EU&ndash;US Data Privacy Framework self-certification.<br/>
				<strong>Site:</strong> <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">cloudflare.com/privacypolicy</a></p>
			</div>
			<div class="feature-card">
				<h3>GitHub, Inc. (Microsoft)</h3>
				<p><strong>Role:</strong> Source-code hosting for the Vectis Mail repository (which is the basis of the product you install).<br/>
				<strong>Location:</strong> United States.<br/>
				<strong>When this is relevant to you:</strong> Only if you choose to interact with us on GitHub (issues, pull requests, discussions). GitHub has its own privacy policy.<br/>
				<strong>Site:</strong> <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">github.com privacy</a></p>
			</div>
		</div>

		<p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">We do not share your information with anyone else for marketing, profiling, or any other purpose. If a court of competent jurisdiction served us with a valid legal demand we would comply with our obligations, document it, and (where lawful) notify the affected person.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">7. International data transfers</h2>
		<p>Veltara Works operates from Australia, but our processors are international. By using vectismail.com or by buying a Vectis Pro subscription, your information may be transferred to or stored in jurisdictions outside Australia, including the United States (Stripe, Cloudflare, GitHub) and the global edge networks operated by Cloudflare. For transfers from the EU, UK, or Switzerland, the relevant safeguards are:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li><strong>Stripe</strong> &mdash; EU&ndash;US Data Privacy Framework (DPF) plus Standard Contractual Clauses for transfers not covered by DPF.</li>
			<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; EU&ndash;US DPF certification plus Standard Contractual Clauses; transfer-impact-assessment documentation is publicly maintained.</li>
			<li><strong>GitHub (Microsoft)</strong> &mdash; EU&ndash;US DPF certification plus Standard Contractual Clauses.</li>
			<li><strong>Veltara Works (Australia)</strong> &mdash; the OAIC has determined Australia provides comparable protections for personal information processed under the Australian Privacy Principles, but we additionally rely on SCCs for any incoming transfer from a jurisdiction that requires them.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">8. How long we keep information</h2>
		<table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.95rem;">
			<thead>
				<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-4);">
					<th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Information</th>
					<th style="text-align: left; padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Retention</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);">
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Cloudflare access logs (IPs, request lines)</td>
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Up to 30 days at the Cloudflare edge, then discarded.</td>
				</tr>
				<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);">
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Contact-form submissions &amp; resulting email threads</td>
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">As long as the conversation remains useful for support and product memory; routinely pruned after 24 months of inactivity unless related to a paid subscription, in which case we keep the thread for the life of the subscription plus 7 years for Australian tax and contract-law reasons.</td>
				</tr>
				<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);">
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Subscription / billing records (with ValidonX)</td>
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">7 years from the end of the financial year in which the last transaction occurred, in line with Australian tax-record obligations.</td>
				</tr>
				<tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);">
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Operational logs on mail.vectismail.com (the mail server itself)</td>
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">30 days, after which they roll out of the log index automatically.</td>
				</tr>
				<tr>
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">Audit-log records of admin actions on our internal mail-admin UI</td>
					<td style="padding: 0.75rem 0.5rem;">90 days, then pruned automatically.</td>
				</tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
		<p style="margin-top: 1rem;">You can ask us at any time how long we currently hold information about you specifically; we'll tell you and, on request, delete it (subject to the legal-retention obligations called out above).</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">9. Your rights</h2>
		<p>Regardless of where you live, we will honour any reasonable request to:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li><strong>Access</strong> the personal information we hold about you.</li>
			<li><strong>Correct</strong> anything that's wrong.</li>
			<li><strong>Delete</strong> what we hold &mdash; with the exception of records we're legally required to keep (mostly billing and tax records).</li>
			<li><strong>Object</strong> to a particular use, or <strong>restrict</strong> processing while we investigate a complaint.</li>
			<li><strong>Receive a portable copy</strong> in a common machine-readable format (CSV or JSON).</li>
			<li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time where consent was the basis for processing.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Email <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a> with "Privacy" in the subject line and a brief description of what you're asking for. We may need to verify your identity (typically by replying from the email address we hold for you) before we act on a request.</p>
		<p>If we've not handled a privacy concern of yours adequately, you can complain to:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li><strong>Australia:</strong> the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC) &mdash; <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au/privacy/privacy-complaints" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">oaic.gov.au</a></li>
			<li><strong>EU/EEA:</strong> the data-protection authority in your country.</li>
			<li><strong>UK:</strong> the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) &mdash; <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">ico.org.uk</a></li>
			<li><strong>California (USA):</strong> the California Privacy Protection Agency (CPPA) &mdash; <a href="https://cppa.ca.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">cppa.ca.gov</a></li>
		</ul>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">10. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
		<p>We use the absolute minimum:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li><strong>Strictly necessary, set by Cloudflare:</strong> a short-lived <code>__cf_bm</code> cookie to distinguish human visitors from automated bot traffic. This is set on every page load and expires within 30 minutes.</li>
			<li><strong>Set by us:</strong> none. The marketing site is fully static, and the only first-party state we use is what your browser already retains for any HTTPS connection.</li>
			<li><strong>Set if you authenticate to <code>mail.vectismail.com</code></strong> (our own use of the product as a customer-support inbox): standard session cookies bound to that mailbox. Customers don't authenticate there.</li>
		</ul>
		<p>Because we don't run advertising or analytics cookies, there is no cookie banner. If we ever introduce a cookie that requires consent under EU/UK law we will surface a granular consent control before it loads, and we will revise this policy.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">11. How we protect your information</h2>
		<p>The technical baseline we operate to:</p>
		<ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
			<li>All traffic to and from vectismail.com runs over TLS 1.2 or higher, with HSTS preload.</li>
			<li>The mail server that handles our internal correspondence (<code>mail.vectismail.com</code>) is itself a Vectis Mail Pro install, kept on the current stable release.</li>
			<li>Passwords (for our own admin accounts) are hashed with Argon2id.</li>
			<li>TOTP secrets and backup material are encrypted at rest with AES-256-GCM.</li>
			<li>We use the principle of least privilege internally: the database role used by the mail server's outward-facing components is read-only.</li>
		</ul>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">12. Children</h2>
		<p>Vectis Mail is a product for businesses and technical operators. It's not intended for, or marketed to, anyone under the age of 16. We don't knowingly collect personal information from children. If you believe a child has provided us information, please write to <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a> and we'll delete it.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">13. Changes to this policy</h2>
		<p>We'll bump the "Last updated" date at the top of this page whenever we change it. For changes that affect how we use information about existing customers (rare), we'll also email you. The current text is always the authoritative version.</p>

		<h2 style="margin-top: 2.5rem;">14. Contact us</h2>
		<p>Email <a href="mailto:support@vectismail.com" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">support@vectismail.com</a> with "Privacy" in the subject line, or use the form at <a href="/contact" style="color: var(--sl-color-accent);">/contact</a> and select Technical Support. We answer.</p>
